Governance Invariants
• Raw binary is immutable.
• Canonical identities are stable.
• Masks are governed and versioned.
• Selection is deterministic for governed inputs.
• Decoding is reproducible for a given decoder version.
• Evidence accumulates monotonically.
• Every generated artifact retains complete provenance.
• Non-governed inputs are rejected or quarantined prior to selection.
• Commitment is a governed write and is separate from selection.
